  names (a table of text)
  stops (a list of numbers)
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- helpers

to joined path, given base (text) and name (text), returning text:
  if base ends with "\" or base ends with "/": return base plus name
  if base begins with "/": return base plus "/" plus name
  return base plus "\" plus name
and the universe said i love you

to short name of, given path (text), returning text:
  set cut to 0
  for each n from 1 to the size of path:
    if letter n of path is one of ("\", "/"): set cut to n
  return letters (cut plus 1) to (the size of path) of path
and the universe said i love you

to spaces, given count (a number), returning text:
  set made to ""
  repeat count times:
    set made to made plus " "
  return made
and the universe said i love you

to leading spaces of, given line (text), returning a number:
  set count to 0
  for each n from 1 to the size of line:
    if letter n of line is not " ": return count
    set count to count plus 1
  return count
and the universe said i love you

to is word letter, given c (text), returning yes or no:
  return "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ'0123456789" contains c and c is not ""
and the universe said i love you

to whole text, returning text:
  return join body with new line
and the universe said i love you

to ask the system, given route (text), returning text:
  return web page route
and the universe said i love you

to tell the system, given route (text) and message (text), returning text:
  return send to the web page with (route, message)
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- colouring a line

to learn the classes:
  for each w in ("if otherwise repeat times for each in from by try return returning given usually whenever every depending cease break free move on went wrong meanwhile anything else") split by " ":
    set entry w of classes to "c-flow"
  for each w in ("scrawl set to ask into add remove inscribe save load conjure as invoke etch consume reveal raise an error with the command") split by " ":
    if not (classes contains w): set entry w of classes to "c-action"
  for each w in ("yes no nothing birth existence horizontal vertical depth wound") split by " ":
    set entry w of classes to "c-constant"
  for each w in ("number text list table place kind thing") split by " ":
    set entry w of classes to "c-kind"
and the universe said i love you

to span, given look (text) and words (text), returning text:
  if words is "": return ""
  return "<span class=" plus a quotation mark plus look plus a quotation mark plus ">" plus safe markup of words plus "</span>"
and the universe said i love you

to coloured words, given line (text), returning text:
  set made to ""
  set n to 1
  set count to the size of line
  as long as n is at most count:
    set c to letter n of line
    if c is a quotation mark:
      set finish to n plus 1
      as long as finish is at most count and letter finish of line is not a quotation mark:
        set finish to finish plus 1
      set made to made plus span with ("c-string", letters n to (smaller of finish and count) of line)
      set n to finish plus 1
    otherwise if "0123456789" contains c:
      set finish to n
      as long as finish is at most count and "0123456789." contains letter finish of line:
        set finish to finish plus 1
      set made to made plus span with ("c-number", letters n to (finish minus 1) of line)
      set n to finish
    otherwise if is word letter with c:
      set finish to n
      as long as finish is at most count and is word letter with (letter finish of line):
        set finish to finish plus 1
      set w to letters n to (finish minus 1) of line
      if classes contains w:
        set made to made plus span with (entry w of classes, w)
      otherwise:
        set made to made plus safe markup of w
      set n to finish
    otherwise:
      set made to made plus safe markup of c
      set n to n plus 1
  return made
and the universe said i love you

to coloured, given line (text), returning text:
  if painted contains line: return entry line of painted
  set t to trimmed line
  set made to ""
  if t begins with "whisper:" or t begins with "note:":
    set made to span with ("c-comment", line)
  otherwise if line is "and the universe said i love you":
    set made to span with ("c-closing", line)
  otherwise if line is one of ("genesis:", "the world remembers:") or line begins with "use:":
    set made to span with ("c-heading", line)
  otherwise if line begins with "to " and line ends with ":":
    set cut to the size of line
    for each n from (the size of line) to 4 by -1:
      if letter n of line is ",": set cut to n
    set made to span with ("c-heading", "to ") plus span with ("c-command", letters 4 to (cut minus 1) of line) plus coloured words with (letters cut to (the size of line) of line)
  otherwise if (line begins with "a " or line begins with "an ") and (line ends with " has:" or line contains " is a kind of "):
    set made to span with ("c-kind", line)
  otherwise:
    set made to coloured words with line
  if the size of painted exceeds 5000: set painted to a table of text
  set entry line of painted to made
  return made
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- the selection

to selecting, returning yes or no:
  return mark row is not row or mark column is not column
and the universe said i love you

to mark comes first, returning yes or no:
  return mark row falls below row or (mark row is row and mark column falls below column)
and the universe said i love you

to start row, returning a number:
  if mark comes first: return mark row
  return row
and the universe said i love you

to start column, returning a number:
  if mark comes first: return mark column
  return column
and the universe said i love you

to end row, returning a number:
  if mark comes first: return row
  return mark row
and the universe said i love you

to end column, returning a number:
  if mark comes first: return column
  return mark column
and the universe said i love you

to chosen words, returning text:
  if not selecting: return ""
  set opening to start row
  set closing to end row
  if opening is closing: return letters (start column) to (end column minus 1) of item opening of body
  set made to letters (start column) to (the size of item opening of body) of item opening of body
  for each r from (opening plus 1) to (closing minus 1):
    set made to made plus new line plus item r of body
  return made plus new line plus letters 1 to (end column minus 1) of item closing of body
and the universe said i love you

to drop the mark:
  set mark row to row
  set mark column to column
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- changing the text (all through 'put words')

to swap lines, given top row (a number) and taking (a number) and putting (a list of text):
  whisper: the lines from top row on (taking of them) become putting
  set made to items 1 to (top row minus 1) of body
  for each line in putting:
    add line to made
  for each r from (top row plus taking) to (the size of body):
    add item r of body to made
  set body to made
and the universe said i love you

to put words, given what (text):
  set fresh to replace (the letter with code 9) with "  " in (replace (the letter with code 13) with "" in what)
  set single to the size of fresh is 1 and fresh is not " " and not selecting
  set was row to row
  set was column to column
  set opening to start row
  set closing to end row
  set before to letters 1 to (start column minus 1) of item opening of body
  set behind to letters (end column) to (the size of item closing of body) of item closing of body
  set pieces to fresh split by new line
  set fitted to a list of text
  for each k from 1 to the size of pieces:
    set piece to item k of pieces
    if k is 1: set piece to before plus piece
    if k is the size of pieces:
      set row to opening plus k minus 1
      set column to (the size of piece) plus 1
      set piece to piece plus behind
    add piece to fitted
  whisper: undo keeps only changed lines; typing on one line is one step
  set merged to no
  if single and typing run and opening is closing and the size of back exceeds 0:
    set last one to the size of back
    if the changed row of item last one of back is opening and the size of the new lines of item last one of back is 1:
      set the new lines of item last one of back to fitted
      set the forth row of item last one of back to row
      set the forth column of item last one of back to column
      set merged to yes
  if not merged:
    conjure a snapshot as moment
    set the changed row of moment to opening
    set the old lines of moment to items opening to closing of body
    set the new lines of moment to fitted
    set the back row of moment to was row
    set the back column of moment to was column
    set the forth row of moment to row
    set the forth column of moment to column
    add moment to back
    if the size of back exceeds 1000: remove item 1 from back
  set ahead to a list of snapshots
  set typing run to single
  swap lines with (opening, closing minus opening plus 1, fitted)
  drop the mark
  set goal column to column
  something changed
and the universe said i love you

to something changed:
  set calm to 0
  set needs look to yes
  set edits to edits plus 1
  measure the widest
  show
and the universe said i love you

to measure the widest:
  set widest to 0
  for each line in body:
    if the size of line exceeds widest: set widest to the size of line
  set the style with (rows box, "width", ((64 plus (widest plus 6) times glyph width) as text) plus "px")
  set the style with (rows box, "height", (((the size of body) times 20) as text) plus "px")
and the universe said i love you

to step, given moment (a snapshot) and undoing (yes or no):
  if undoing:
    swap lines with (the changed row of moment, the size of the new lines of moment, the old lines of moment)
    set row to the back row of moment
    set column to the back column of moment
  otherwise:
    swap lines with (the changed row of moment, the size of the old lines of moment, the new lines of moment)
    set row to the forth row of moment
    set column to the forth column of moment
  set row to clamp row between 1 and (the size of body)
  set column to clamp column between 1 and ((the size of item row of body) plus 1)
  drop the mark
  set goal column to column
  set typing run to no
  something changed
and the universe said i love you

to undo:
  if the size of back is 0: cease
  set moment to last item of back
  remove item (the size of back) from back
  add moment to ahead
  step with (moment, yes)
and the universe said i love you

to redo:
  if the size of ahead is 0: cease
  set moment to last item of ahead
  remove item (the size of ahead) from ahead
  add moment to back
  step with (moment, no)
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- moving the caret

to go to, given r (a number) and c (a number) and keeping (yes or no):
  set row to clamp r between 1 and (the size of body)
  set column to clamp c between 1 and ((the size of item row of body) plus 1)
  if not keeping: drop the mark
  set typing run to no
  show
and the universe said i love you

to go up or down, given count (a number) and keeping (yes or no):
  set goal to goal column
  go to with (row plus count, goal, keeping)
  set goal column to goal
and the universe said i love you

to go across, given count (a number) and keeping (yes or no):
  if selecting and not keeping:
    if count falls below 0: go to with (start row, start column, no)
    otherwise: go to with (end row, end column, no)
  otherwise if count falls below 0 and column is 1 and row exceeds 1:
    go to with (row minus 1, (the size of item (row minus 1) of body) plus 1, keeping)
  otherwise if count exceeds 0 and column exceeds the size of item row of body and row falls below the size of body:
    go to with (row plus 1, 1, keeping)
  otherwise:
    go to with (row, column plus count, keeping)
  set goal column to column
and the universe said i love you

to word edge, given forward (yes or no), returning a number:
  set line to item row of body
  set c to column
  if forward:
    as long as c is at most the size of line and not is word letter with (letter c of line):
      set c to c plus 1
    as long as c is at most the size of line and is word letter with (letter c of line):
      set c to c plus 1
    return c
  as long as c exceeds 1 and not is word letter with (letter (c minus 1) of line):
    set c to c minus 1
  as long as c exceeds 1 and is word letter with (letter (c minus 1) of line):
    set c to c minus 1
  return c
and the universe said i love you

to select the word here:
  set line to item row of body
  set opening to column
  as long as opening exceeds 1 and is word letter with (letter (opening minus 1) of line):
    set opening to opening minus 1
  set closing to column
  as long as closing is at most the size of line and is word letter with (letter closing of line):
    set closing to closing plus 1
  set mark row to row
  set mark column to opening
  set column to closing
  show
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- drawing the box

to show:
  if current is 0: cease
  set left to 64 plus (column minus 1) times glyph width
  set top to (row minus 1) times 20
  set the style with (caret box, "left", (left as text) plus "px")
  set the style with (caret box, "top", (top as text) plus "px")
  set the style with (catcher, "left", (left as text) plus "px")
  set the style with (catcher, "top", (top as text) plus "px")
  show the marks
  if selecting:
    set the value with (catcher, chosen words)
    select all in the element catcher
  otherwise:
    set the value with (catcher, "")
  scroll into view caret box
  paint the rows
  set the text with (where box, "Line " plus row plus ", Column " plus column)
  set the text with (mistake box, "")
  for each k from 1 to the size of mistake rows:
    if item k of mistake rows is row: set the text with (mistake box, item k of mistake notes)
  show the tabs
and the universe said i love you

to paint the rows:
  whisper: only rows in sight are drawn
  if current is 0: cease
  set scrolled to scrolled down in the element code box
  set shown start to larger of 1 and ((round down (scrolled divided by 20)) minus 4)
  set shown end to smaller of (the size of body) and (shown start plus (round down ((the height of code box) divided by 20)) plus 9)
  set made to ""
  for each r from shown start to shown end:
    set look to "row"
    if r is row: set look to look plus " here"
    if mistake rows contains r: set look to look plus " bad"
    if stop rows contains r: set look to look plus " stop"
    if paused and r is paused row: set look to look plus " paused"
    set made to made plus "<div class=" plus a quotation mark plus look plus a quotation mark plus "><span class=" plus a quotation mark plus "num" plus a quotation mark plus ">" plus r plus "</span><span class=" plus a quotation mark plus "txt" plus a quotation mark plus ">" plus coloured with (item r of body) plus "</span></div>"
  set the markup with (rows box, "<div class=" plus a quotation mark plus "shown" plus a quotation mark plus " style=" plus a quotation mark plus "top:" plus ((shown start minus 1) times 20) plus "px" plus a quotation mark plus ">" plus made plus "</div>")
and the universe said i love you

to on scroll, given event (a number):
  paint the rows
and the universe said i love you

to show the marks:
  set made to ""
  if selecting:
    for each r from start row to end row:
      set opening to 1
      if r is start row: set opening to start column
      set closing to (the size of item r of body) plus 2
      if r is end row: set closing to end column
      if closing exceeds opening:
        set made to made plus "<div class=" plus a quotation mark plus "mark" plus a quotation mark plus " style=" plus a quotation mark plus "left:" plus (64 plus (opening minus 1) times glyph width) plus "px;top:" plus ((r minus 1) times 20) plus "px;width:" plus ((closing minus opening) times glyph width) plus "px" plus a quotation mark plus "></div>"
  set the markup with (marks box, made)
and the universe said i love you

to spot of the pointer, given event (a number):
  set x to (the pointer x coordinate of event) minus (the left edge of rows box) minus 64
  set y to (the pointer y coordinate of event) minus (the top edge of rows box)
  set row to clamp ((round down (y divided by 20)) plus 1) between 1 and (the size of body)
  set column to clamp ((round (x divided by glyph width)) plus 1) between 1 and ((the size of item row of body) plus 1)
  set goal column to column
  set typing run to no
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---------------------------------------------------------------- keys

to on key, given event (a number):
  set key to key of the event event
  set control to control held in the event event
  set shift to shift held in the event event
  whisper: held back so commands on the page run in turn
  set handled to key is one of ("ArrowLeft", "ArrowRight", "ArrowUp", "ArrowDown", "Home", "End", "PageUp", "PageDown", "Backspace", "Delete", "Enter", "Tab", "Escape", "F5", "F6", "F7", "F8", "F9", "F10", "F11")
  if control and not (key is one of ("c", "x", "v", "C", "X", "V", "Control")): set handled to yes
  if handled: hold back the event event
  if suggesting and key is one of ("ArrowUp", "ArrowDown", "Enter", "Tab", "Escape"):
    if key is "ArrowUp": set chosen to larger of 1 and (chosen minus 1)
    if key is "ArrowDown": set chosen to smaller of (the size of picks) and (chosen plus 1)
    if key is "Escape": hide the suggestions
    if key is "Enter" or key is "Tab": take the pick
    otherwise: show the picks
    cease
  if control and key is one of ("z", "Z"):
    if shift: redo
    otherwise: undo
  otherwise if control and key is one of ("y", "Y"): redo
  otherwise if control and key is one of ("a", "A"):
    set mark row to 1
    set mark column to 1
    set row to the size of body
    set column to (the size of last item of body) plus 1
    show
  otherwise if control and key is one of ("s", "S"): save the sheet
  otherwise if control and key is " ": suggest with yes
  otherwise if control and key is "Home": go to with (1, 1, shift)
  otherwise if control and key is "End": go to with (the size of body, (the size of last item of body) plus 1, shift)
  otherwise if control and key is "ArrowLeft": go to with (row, word edge with no, shift)
  otherwise if control and key is "ArrowRight": go to with (row, word edge with yes, shift)
  otherwise if key is "ArrowLeft": go across with (-1, shift)
  otherwise if key is "ArrowRight": go across with (1, shift)
  otherwise if key is "ArrowUp": go up or down with (-1, shift)
  otherwise if key is "ArrowDown": go up or down with (1, shift)
  otherwise if key is "PageUp": go up or down with (-(round down ((the height of code box) divided by 20)), shift)
  otherwise if key is "PageDown": go up or down with (round down ((the height of code box) divided by 20), shift)
  otherwise if key is "Home":
    set indent to (leading spaces of item row of body) plus 1
    if column is indent: go to with (row, 1, shift)
    otherwise: go to with (row, indent, shift)
  otherwise if key is "End": go to with (row, (the size of item row of body) plus 1, shift)
  otherwise if key is "Backspace":
    if not selecting:
      if column exceeds 1:
        set mark column to column minus 1
        set line to item row of body
        if trimmed (letters 1 to (column minus 1) of line) is "" and column exceeds 2: set mark column to column minus 2
      otherwise if row exceeds 1:
        set mark row to row minus 1
        set mark column to (the size of item mark row of body) plus 1
    put words with ""
  otherwise if key is "Delete":
    if not selecting:
      if column is at most the size of item row of body:
        set mark column to column plus 1
      otherwise if row falls below the size of body:
        set mark row to row plus 1
        set mark column to 1
    put words with ""
  otherwise if key is "Enter":
    set line to item row of body
    set indent to leading spaces of line
    if trimmed (letters 1 to (column minus 1) of line) ends with ":": set indent to indent plus 2
    put words with (new line plus spaces with indent)
  otherwise if key is "Tab":
    if shift:
      set line to item row of body
      if line begins with "  ":
        set keep to column
        set mark column to 1
        set column to 3
        put words with ""
        go to with (row, keep minus 2, no)
    otherwise:
      put words with "  "
  otherwise if key is "Escape": go to with (row, column, no)
  otherwise if paused and key is one of ("F5", "F10", "F11"):
    if key is "F5" and not shift: debug say with "go"
    otherwise if key is "F10": debug say with "over"
    otherwise if key is "F11" and shift: debug say with "out"
    otherwise if key is "F11": debug say with "step"
  otherwise if key is "F9":
    start running with "debug"
  otherwise if key is one of ("F5", "F6", "F7", "F8"):
    if shift and key is "F5": stop running
    otherwise if key is "F5": start running with "run"
    otherwise if key is "F6": start running with "watch"
    otherwise if key is "F7": start running with "test"
    otherwise: start running with "build"
and the universe said i love you

to on typing, given event (a number):
  set got to value of the element catcher
  if selecting and got is chosen words: cease
  put words with got
  if the size of got is 1 and is word letter with got: suggest with no
  otherwise: hide the suggestions
and the universe said i love you

to on press, given event (a number):
  if current is 0: cease
  if the nearest matching element with (the target of event, "#suggest") is not 0: cease
  hold back the event event
  if (the pointer x coordinate of event) minus (the left edge of rows box) falls below 56:
    set y to (the pointer y coordinate of event) minus (the top edge of rows box)
    toggle the stop with (clamp ((round down (y divided by 20)) plus 1) between 1 and (the size of body))
    cease
  focus on the element catcher
  set keep row to mark row
  set keep column to mark column
  spot of the pointer with event
  if shift held in the event event:
    set mark row to keep row
    set mark column to keep column
  otherwise:
    drop the mark
  set dragging to yes
  hide the suggestions
  show
and the universe said i love you

to on pointer move, given event (a number):
  if not dragging: cease
  set keep row to mark row
  set keep column to mark column
  spot of the pointer with event
  set mark row to keep row
  set mark column to keep column
  show
and the universe said i love you

to on let go, given event (a number):
  set dragging to no
and the universe said i love you

to on double press, given event (a number):
  if current is 0: cease
  select the word here
and the universe said i love you

to on wake, given event (a number):
  apply the appearance with (code box, "awake")
and the universe said i love you

to on sleep, given event (a number):
  remove the appearance with (code box, "awake")
  hide the suggestions
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- suggestions

to the word before the caret, returning text:
  set line to item row of body
  set opening to column
  as long as opening exceeds 1 and is word letter with (letter (opening minus 1) of line):
    set opening to opening minus 1
  return letters opening to (column minus 1) of line
and the universe said i love you

to the line before the caret, returning text:
  return trimmed (letters 1 to (column minus 1) of item row of body)
and the universe said i love you

to suggest, given asked (yes or no):
  set w to lower case of (the word before the caret)
  set line to lower case of (the line before the caret)
  if not asked and the size of w falls below 2:
    hide the suggestions
    cease
  set picks to a list of numbers
  for each k from 1 to the size of labels:
    set label to lower case of item k of labels
    if the size of picks falls below 12:
