whisper: ---- the beat: mistakes and output

to tick:
  set calm to calm plus 1
  if needs look and calm is at least 3: look for mistakes
  if running: poll the program
and the universe said i love you

whisper: ---- starting up

to hook up, given selector (text) and happening (text) and then (a command given a number):
  listen for an event with (the element selector, happening, then)
and the universe said i love you

genesis:
  set code box to the element "#code"
  set rows box to the element "#rows"
  set marks box to the element "#marks"
  set caret box to the element "#caret"
  set catcher to the element "#catcher"
  set suggest box to the element "#suggest"
  set tabs box to the element "#tabs"
  set files box to the element "#files"
  set words box to the element "#words"
  set output box to the element "#output"
  set mistakes box to the element "#mistakes"
  set answer box to the element "#answer"
  set status box to the element "#status"
  set where box to the element "#where"
  set mistake box to the element "#mistake-line"
  set glyph width to (the width of (the element "#measure")) divided by 100
  learn the classes
  listen for an event with (catcher, "keydown", the command on key)
  listen for an event with (catcher, "input", the command on typing)
  listen for an event with (catcher, "focus", the command on wake)
  listen for an event with (catcher, "blur", the command on sleep)
  listen for an event with (code box, "mousedown", the command on press)
  listen for an event with (code box, "dblclick", the command on double press)
  listen for an event with (code box, "scroll", the command on scroll)
  listen for an event with (the whole window, "mousemove", the command on pointer move)
  listen for an event with (the whole window, "mouseup", the command on let go)
  listen for an event with (the whole window, "keydown", the command on window key)
  listen for an event with (suggest box, "mousedown", the command on pick press)
  listen for an event with (tabs box, "click", the command on tab press)
  listen for an event with (files box, "click", the command on file press)
  listen for an event with (words box, "click", the command on word press)
  listen for an event with (output box, "click", the command on line press)
  listen for an event with (mistakes box, "click", the command on line press)
  listen for an event with (answer box, "keydown", the command on answer key)
  hook up with ("#word-search", "input", the command on word search)
  hook up with ("#show-output", "click", the command on output tab press)
  hook up with ("#show-mistakes", "click", the command on mistakes tab press)
  hook up with ("#learn", "click", the command on learn press)
  hook up with ("#run", "click", the command on run press)
  hook up with ("#watch", "click", the command on watch press)
  hook up with ("#debug", "click", the command on debug press)
  hook up with ("#profile", "click", the command on profile press)
  hook up with ("#wasm", "click", the command on wasm press)
  hook up with ("#step", "click", the command on step press)
  hook up with ("#over", "click", the command on over press)
  hook up with ("#out", "click", the command on out press)
  hook up with ("#go", "click", the command on go press)
  hook up with ("#test", "click", the command on test press)
  hook up with ("#build", "click", the command on build press)
  hook up with ("#web", "click", the command on web press)
  hook up with ("#stop", "click", the command on stop press)
  hook up with ("#clear", "click", the command on clear press)
  hook up with ("#new-file", "click", the command on new file press)
  hook up with ("#open-folder", "click", the command on open folder press)
  load home from the text (ask the system with "/api/home")
  set folder to joined path with (home, "examples")
  conjure a memory as remembered
  try:
    load remembered from the text (ask the system with "/api/settings")
  if that went wrong:
    conjure a memory as remembered
  if the folder of remembered is not "" and (ask the system with ("/api/exists?path=" plus web encoded (the folder of remembered))) is "true":
    set folder to ask the system with ("/api/opening?path=" plus web encoded (the folder of remembered))
  load the tree
  load the words
  for each path in the files of remembered:
    try:
      open the sheet with path
    if that went wrong:
      set ignored to ""
  every with (0.25, the command tick)
and the universe said i love you
